title: Prefabs inside prefabs
intro: A prefab can hold copies of other prefabs, like gems in a chest. Save the gem, and the gems in every chest follow it.
project: Platformer | Nested Prefabs

chapter: A gem and a chest | Two prefabs
look: 8, -2, 4
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Gem
set: Transform.Position = 5, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #FFEC27
set: Sprite.Size = 0.5, 0.5
add: Pickup
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Chest
set: Transform.Position = 9, -3.2, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #AB5236
set: Sprite.Size = 1.2, 0.8
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
say: A gem and a chest, each saved as a prefab.

chapter: Put a gem in the chest | In the chest's own tab
menu: Entity > Edit Prefab
assetmenu: Prefabs/Gem.prefab > Add to Scene
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0.7, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #FFA300
expectprefab: Gem = Gem
explain: entity:Gem | A gem inside the chest | In the chest's tab, Add to Scene puts a copy of the gem inside the chest. This chest's gem is a darker gold, a change of its own.
save
click: tab:Main
expectcount: Gem = 2

chapter: Change the gem | Every chest's gems follow
select: Gem
menu: Entity > Edit Prefab
set: Pickup.Amount = 5
set: Sprite.Size = 0.7, 0.7
save
explain: tab:Gem | Saved | Saving the gem prefab updates every copy of it: in the scenes, and inside other prefabs too.
click: tab:Chest
expectvalue: Gem.Pickup.Amount = 5
expectvalue: Gem.Sprite.Size.X = 0.7
expectvalue: Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FFA300
explain: entity:Gem | Updated, change kept | The chest's gem is worth five now, and bigger, and it's still the darker gold the chest gave it.
click: tab:Main
expectoverrides: Chest = none
explain: world:4, -1.5, 12, -4.5 | The placed chest too | And the chest placed in the scene is just like its prefab, with no changes of its own to look after.
